<section class="home-guidance" aria-labelledby="home-guidance-title">
  <div class="home-guidance-inner">
    <div class="home-guidance-heading">
      <p class="home-guidance-eyebrow">For solicitors, insurers and professional organisations</p>
      <h2 id="home-guidance-title">Instructing Dr Qureshi</h2>
      <p class="home-guidance-lead">From an initial enquiry to an independent psychiatric expert report, the process begins with understanding the case and agreeing what is needed.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="home-guidance-process">
      <h3>How an instruction works</h3>
      <ol class="home-guidance-steps">
        <li>
          <span class="home-guidance-step-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <div><h4>Availability and conflicts</h4><p>Outline the case and any deadlines so availability can be checked and potential conflicts of interest considered.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="home-guidance-step-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <div><h4>Letter of instruction</h4><p>Agree the scope of the expert opinion, the records to be reviewed, fees and reporting timescales.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="home-guidance-step-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <div><h4>Psychiatric assessment</h4><p>The assessment is arranged in person or by secure video link, where clinically appropriate.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="home-guidance-step-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
          <div><h4>Report and follow-up</h4><p>Reports are typically provided within two to four weeks of assessment. Urgent instructions can be considered; supplementary or joint reports and attendance at proof are available where required.</p></div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="home-guidance-details">
      <div class="home-guidance-detail">
        <h3>Where assessments take place</h3>
        <p>Assessments may be arranged at the Glasgow office, at an agreed venue elsewhere in Scotland, or remotely by secure video link where clinically appropriate.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="home-guidance-detail">
        <h3>Independent expert opinion</h3>
        <p>Dr Qureshi provides impartial psychiatric opinions for pursuer and defender instructions. His overriding duty is to the court or tribunal, not the instructing party.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="home-guidance-note">Medical records and supporting documents should be sent only after a secure transfer method has been agreed. <a href="/instructions">Read more about instructing Dr Qureshi <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
  </div>
</section>

